; Under --group-by-cumulative the postings keep their xdata between groups,
; and with -r a later group is handed again a posting an earlier group
; related.  Each group must list the rows plain --group-by lists for it,
; with the running total (reg) or the account totals (bal) carried over.
; The later groups lost their rows: related_posts kept its received and
; handled marks, and the register its displayed mark, so they skipped
; every posting an earlier group had related.  Once such a posting is
; handed on again, nothing it holds from the earlier visit may count:
;
; - the Expenses:Food group starts with the Grocer's Expenses:Utilities
;   posting, which the Assets:Checking group ended with, so calc_posts
;   must continue from that posting's carried totals before it resets
;   them for this visit (else a bogus <Adjustment> row and a lost total),
;   and the register must print it as the first row of its group, with
;   its date and payee;
; - -V, -X and --lots (no prices here, so they change nothing) cache the
;   display total on the posting, which must not be read on a later visit;
; - -S keeps sort keys on the posting, and a second set appended to the
;   first made the sort fail an assertion;
; - payee_changed is a mark of one display: false on the first row of a
;   transaction, and after a posting of the same payee;
; - the account totals count a posting once (its considered mark), so bal
;   added nothing for the Grocer's Expenses:Utilities posting in the
;   Expenses:Food group and printed a total of $105.00 there; a group's
;   account totals count each of its own postings, as its running total
;   does, so bal equals bal -M and the carried reg total, $110.00;
; - -M marks each posting it subtotals compound, with its bare amount, and
;   with `cleared`, whose amount is a pair, the later group added that bare
;   amount to a pair ("Cannot add sequences of different lengths").

2012/01/15 Electric Company
    Expenses:Utilities          $50.00
    Assets:Checking

2012/02/15 Electric Company
    Expenses:Utilities          $55.00
    Assets:Checking

2012/02/20 Grocer
    Expenses:Food               $20.00
    Expenses:Utilities           $5.00  ; Payee: Electric Company
    Assets:Checking

test reg --group-by account -r
Assets:Checking
12-Jan-15 Electric Company      Expenses:Utilities           $50.00       $50.00
12-Feb-15 Electric Company      Expenses:Utilities           $55.00      $105.00
12-Feb-20 Grocer                Expenses:Food                $20.00      $125.00
          Electric Company      Expenses:Utilities            $5.00      $130.00

Expenses:Food
12-Feb-20 Electric Company      Expenses:Utilities            $5.00        $5.00
          Grocer                Assets:Checking             $-25.00      $-20.00

Expenses:Utilities
12-Jan-15 Electric Company      Assets:Checking             $-50.00      $-50.00
12-Feb-15 Electric Company      Assets:Checking             $-55.00     $-105.00
12-Feb-20 Grocer                Expenses:Food                $20.00      $-85.00
                                Assets:Checking             $-25.00     $-110.00
end test

